<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Confederation of Shan States</h1><p class="st-meta">1527 CE – 1555 CE · capital Ava</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An alliance of Shan principalities led by Mohnyin that conquered Ava in 1527 and ruled Upper Burma until Bayinnaung's conquest.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Shan saophas had raided the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ava-kingdom">Ava Kingdom</a> for decades. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sawlon">Sawlon of Mohnyin</a>, a coalition of Shan states including <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mohnyin">Mohnyin</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mogaung">Mogaung</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhamo">Bhamo</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/momeik-state">Momeik</a> and Kale attacked Ava and in 1527 captured it, killing King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shwenankyawshin">Shwenankyawshin</a>. Sawlon placed his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thohanbwa">Thohanbwa</a> on the throne.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederation ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-burma">Upper Burma</a> from Ava but remained a loose alliance of Shan rulers with their own interests. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thohanbwa">Thohanbwa</a> distrusted the Burmese Buddhist establishment and is remembered in the chronicles for killing monks and destroying pagodas, though this may be exaggerated. The confederation allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prome-kingdom">Prome Kingdom</a> against the rising Toungoo.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thohanbwa">Thohanbwa</a> was assassinated in 1542, and Ava passed to other Shan and Burman nobles. Internal quarrels weakened the alliance, and in 1555 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayinnaung">Bayinnaung</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-toungoo-empire">First Toungoo Empire</a> captured Ava, then subdued the northern Shan states one by one.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/confederation-of-shan-states.jpg" alt="Confederation of Shan States" width="320" height="368"><figcaption>Image: User:Jolle · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shan_States-Map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1527 CE – 1555 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ava</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sawlon, Thohanbwa, Hkonmaing</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Shan, Burmese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Shan Confederation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1541&amp;focus=confederation-of-shan-states" aria-label="Confederation of Shan States on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7252 1380 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Confederation of Shan States lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7574 1626h0M7609 1732h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7572 1636h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7572 1636h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Myanmar. <a href="/atlas?year=1541&amp;focus=confederation-of-shan-states">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
